INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('1cc52c70-d88d-5239-8c62-bc2b44c4a769', '9502cd4e-e337-53f0-8fc3-60cdd86658d9', 'a4b09526-14c9-5fd2-ba05-123f07de2857', 'Client-server architecture and HTTP', 'Overview
Learn how web clients communicate with backend servers over HTTP using request methods, status codes, and headers.

What you''ll learn
- HTTP Request Lifecycle
- Methods and Headers

Subtopics
HTTP Request Lifecycle: How DNS resolution, TCP handshakes, and HTTP requests flow from client to server.
Methods and Headers: The semantic purpose of GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, and common request/response headers.

Learning outcome
Understand client-server architecture and http, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Use curl or Postman to inspect headers and status codes of an existing public API endpoint.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: use curl or postman to inspect headers and status codes of an existing public api endpoint. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
