INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('62b9f9d8-1cde-5d69-844c-f535c1245098', '9502cd4e-e337-53f0-8fc3-60cdd86658d9', 'e496d555-bff1-5461-9af9-09c9ef288ac6', 'Containerizing backend services with Docker', 'Overview
Package backend code, runtime dependencies, and configuration into consistent, portable Docker container images.

What you''ll learn
- Dockerfile Directives
- Multi-Stage Builds

Subtopics
Dockerfile Directives: Using FROM, WORKDIR, COPY, RUN, CMD, and non-root users for secure, reproducible builds.
Multi-Stage Builds: Minimizing production image size by separating compilation tools from runtime images.

Learning outcome
Understand containerizing backend services with docker, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Write a multi-stage Dockerfile that builds and runs your backend application in a slim Linux container.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: write a multi-stage dockerfile that builds and runs your backend application in a slim linux container. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
