INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('74808f92-dc89-55d5-b296-e80bd65bd659', 'f8195ff4-7b82-5806-af00-c6a3d0e9ec01', '1e3fd807-8014-5c28-a4f1-a96c7034624f', 'Full-stack web architecture', 'Overview
Learn how client applications, server APIs, and database tiers interact to deliver full-stack user experiences.

What you''ll learn
- Multi-Tier Architecture
- Data Flow Patterns

Subtopics
Multi-Tier Architecture: The roles of browser clients, edge caches, application servers, and persistence layers.
Data Flow Patterns: How user interactions trigger network requests, server processing, and reactive UI updates.

Learning outcome
Understand full-stack web architecture, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Diagram the complete data flow of a user submitting a comment form on a full-stack blog.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: diagram the complete data flow of a user submitting a comment form on a full-stack blog. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
