INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('fb60c74d-6908-5b36-9bf3-923913c79abc', 'eed0cf4d-f4c7-583f-8356-aa8603406a8d', 'fa4f2917-ce5d-5b35-b6a8-9e930d7297db', 'Game engine architecture and the game loop', 'Overview
Learn how the game loop handles input, updates game state, and renders frames at consistent target frame rates.

What you''ll learn
- The Game Loop
- Delta Time

Subtopics
The Game Loop: How initialization, input processing, physics step, state update, and rendering execute every frame.
Delta Time: Using delta time (time between frames) to ensure movement speed is independent of hardware frame rate.

Learning outcome
Understand game engine architecture and the game loop, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Implement a minimal game loop in code that logs frame duration and moves an object based on delta time.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: implement a minimal game loop in code that logs frame duration and moves an object based on delta time. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
