INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('c6b29355-2aeb-51c2-8d8a-41c95b70afd0', 'eed0cf4d-f4c7-583f-8356-aa8603406a8d', 'fa4f2917-ce5d-5b35-b6a8-9e930d7297db', 'Coordinates, transforms and vectors', 'Overview
Master 2D and 3D coordinate systems, position transforms, vector arithmetic (addition, normalization, dot product).

What you''ll learn
- Vector Math for Games
- Local vs World Space

Subtopics
Vector Math for Games: Calculating distance between objects, normalizing direction vectors, and calculating velocities.
Local vs World Space: Understanding parent-child transform hierarchies and rotating relative to world axes.

Learning outcome
Understand coordinates, transforms and vectors, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Write a script that calculates the normalized direction vector and distance from an enemy to the player.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: write a script that calculates the normalized direction vector and distance from an enemy to the player. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
