Structure complex character behaviors cleanly using finite state machines (FSM) separating Idle, Walk, Jump, and Attack.

What you''ll learn
- State Machine Architecture
- Transition Logic

Subtopics
State Machine Architecture: Defining distinct state classes with enter, update, and exit lifecycle hooks.
Transition Logic: Switching states cleanly when conditions are met (e.g., falling velocity switches to Fall state).

Learning outcome
Understand finite state machines for characters, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Build a state machine for an enemy with Patrol, Chase, and Attack states based on distance to player.

Completion check
