Troubleshoot physics tunneling, erratic collisions, orphaned nodes in the scene tree, and memory leaks.

What you''ll learn
- Continuous Collision Detection (CCD)
- Orphaned Node Cleanup

Subtopics
Continuous Collision Detection (CCD): Preventing fast-moving projectiles from tunneling through thin walls.
Orphaned Node Cleanup: Ensuring scenes free dynamically spawned nodes when removed from the scene tree.

Learning outcome
Understand debugging game physics and memory leaks, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Enable visual collision debugging, inspect physics shapes during runtime, and verify that destroyed objects are freed.

Completion check
