INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('2001a23d-698a-567c-9bac-0e89c3f516c6', '2747fd69-c19e-5bc0-8072-db5a001a424f', 'a5ae4fe7-0ad4-5919-be1b-5ce8c4cf043c', 'Prompt design, few-shot learning and system prompts', 'Overview
Master zero-shot, few-shot prompting, chain-of-thought reasoning, and crafting role-based system instructions.

What you''ll learn
- System vs User Prompts
- Few-Shot In-Context Learning

Subtopics
System vs User Prompts: Setting behavioral constraints and domain personas in system messages.
Few-Shot In-Context Learning: Providing high-quality input-output examples directly in the prompt context.

Learning outcome
Understand prompt design, few-shot learning and system prompts, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Write a system prompt with few-shot examples that reliably extracts structured invoice data from unstructured text.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: write a system prompt with few-shot examples that reliably extracts structured invoice data from unstructured text. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
