INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('cf28f663-524c-5c39-83ac-2a3e4a065a1e', '2747fd69-c19e-5bc0-8072-db5a001a424f', '75d19ea5-51f6-5560-9391-1e4a21f14f54', 'End-to-end RAG architecture', 'Overview
Connect user queries, semantic retrieval, prompt synthesis, and grounded LLM generation into a unified RAG workflow.

What you''ll learn
- The RAG Pipeline
- Reducing Hallucinations

Subtopics
The RAG Pipeline: Retrieving relevant context from vector stores, injecting it into prompts, and asking the LLM to answer.
Reducing Hallucinations: Instructing models to answer strictly based on retrieved context and admit when information is missing.

Learning outcome
Understand end-to-end rag architecture, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Build a working RAG script that takes a user question, retrieves relevant chunks, and returns an answer citing sources.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: build a working rag script that takes a user question, retrieves relevant chunks, and returns an answer citing sources. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
