INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('b63eff79-3db4-532c-b1d7-a5ef6f67f1e6', '91339a49-2836-5360-9d4e-b84b68769e2c', '955fbb6f-a8e8-5e41-8446-af7f7ff5f4ec', 'Python numerical programming with NumPy', 'Overview
Perform high-performance numerical computations using N-dimensional arrays, vectorization, and mathematical operations.

What you''ll learn
- Ndarray Manipulation
- Vectorized Operations

Subtopics
Ndarray Manipulation: Creating arrays, slicing multi-dimensional data, and reshaping matrices.
Vectorized Operations: Writing vectorized mathematical expressions that replace slow Python loops.

Learning outcome
Understand python numerical programming with numpy, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Write vectorized NumPy expressions to normalize a 2D matrix of numbers to zero mean and unit variance.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: write vectorized numpy expressions to normalize a 2d matrix of numbers to zero mean and unit variance. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
