Detect missing values, apply imputation techniques (mean, median, forward fill), and cast appropriate data types.

What you''ll learn
- Missingness Patterns
- Imputation Strategies

Subtopics
Missingness Patterns: Distinguishing between Missing Completely at Random (MCAR) and Missing at Random (MAR).
Imputation Strategies: Choosing between row deletion, simple median imputation, and model-based imputation.

Learning outcome
Understand handling missing data and type casting, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Impute missing numeric values in a DataFrame with the median and fill missing categorical values with the mode.

