Design clear, actionable Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) like customer churn, lifetime value (LTV), and revenue growth.

What you''ll learn
- Leading vs Lagging Indicators
- SMART Metric Criteria

Subtopics
Leading vs Lagging Indicators: Distinguishing between predictive input metrics and outcome results.
SMART Metric Criteria: Ensuring KPIs are Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant, and Time-bound.

Learning outcome
Understand defining business kpis and metric frameworks, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Draft a KPI dictionary defining 5 key metrics for an e-commerce business including formula, data sources, and targets.

Completion check
