INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('5653240d-3a05-57eb-b1d4-5248b4366f7f', 'edfa68df-4a87-52a5-afe6-7cf2537d616b', 'db75bbe1-8358-5455-8196-e7849b55f02b', 'Global infrastructure: regions and availability zones', 'Overview
Understand how cloud providers structure regions, multiple independent availability zones (AZs), and edge locations.

What you''ll learn
- Regions and Availability Zones
- Edge Locations and Latency

Subtopics
Regions and Availability Zones: Why deploying across multiple AZs provides fault tolerance against localized data center outages.
Edge Locations and Latency: Using edge points of presence (PoP) to cache content close to global end users.

Learning outcome
Understand global infrastructure: regions and availability zones, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Draft a multi-AZ deployment plan for a web app that remains available if an entire availability zone experiences a blackout.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: draft a multi-az deployment plan for a web app that remains available if an entire availability zone experiences a blackout. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
