INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('dbfd4115-9c7e-5a20-a3a0-6365b6fd7b13', 'edfa68df-4a87-52a5-afe6-7cf2537d616b', '4c65bd23-64b1-55d1-977e-971c2e327302', 'Cloud metrics, alarms and log aggregation', 'Overview
Collect system metrics (CPU, disk I/O, network), aggregate application logs, and trigger SNS alerts on anomalous spikes.

What you''ll learn
- Metric Alarms
- Centralized Log Groups

Subtopics
Metric Alarms: Configuring alarms that trigger automated actions when error rates or CPU cross thresholds.
Centralized Log Groups: Streaming container and OS logs to central log stores for real-time querying and filtering.

Learning outcome
Understand cloud metrics, alarms and log aggregation, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Create a metric alarm that sends an alert notification if server CPU utilization exceeds 80% for 5 consecutive minutes.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: create a metric alarm that sends an alert notification if server cpu utilization exceeds 80% for 5 consecutive minutes. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
