INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('af988d84-3e31-502d-b924-79daf245257d', '5df0777c-53ba-5a29-9b9d-e290bae381bc', 'db890574-d59e-5815-a662-57ea25accf11', 'Linux distribution families and installation', 'Overview
Learn the differences between Debian/Ubuntu and RHEL/Fedora distribution families, kernel releases, and minimal server installations.

What you''ll learn
- Distribution Ecosystems
- Headless Server Installation

Subtopics
Distribution Ecosystems: Comparing package formats (.deb vs .rpm), release cadences (LTS vs rolling), and enterprise support.
Headless Server Installation: Installing a minimal server operating system without graphical desktop overhead.

Learning outcome
Understand linux distribution families and installation, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Install a minimal headless Linux server in a local virtual machine and log in via the console.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: install a minimal headless linux server in a local virtual machine and log in via the console. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
