Master the Filesystem Hierarchy Standard (FHS), understanding the roles of /etc, /var, /home, /usr, /tmp, and /opt.

What you''ll learn
- The Linux Directory Tree
- Absolute vs Relative Paths

Subtopics
The Linux Directory Tree: Where configuration files (/etc), system logs (/var/log), and binaries (/usr/bin) reside.
Absolute vs Relative Paths: Navigating directory structures efficiently using cd, ls -la, pwd, and tree.

Learning outcome
Understand filesystem hierarchy and navigation, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Explore the root filesystem, locate the system hosts file in /etc, and inspect recent log files in /var/log.

Completion check
