Harness the power of the command line using standard streams (stdin, stdout, stderr), pipes (|), and file redirection operators.

What you''ll learn
- Standard Streams and Redirection
- Piping and Text Filters

Subtopics
Standard Streams and Redirection: Redirecting command output to files with > and >>, and capturing error streams with 2>&1.
Piping and Text Filters: Chaining commands together using grep, sort, uniq, cut, and wc to extract information.

Learning outcome
Understand shell commands, pipes and text redirection, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Write a command pipeline that extracts all unique usernames from /etc/passwd sorted alphabetically.

Completion check
