INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('5999f08e-16f6-5fb2-9503-2f7138868377', '5df0777c-53ba-5a29-9b9d-e290bae381bc', '67fd078b-a17d-5bfa-b131-f310b10f8327', 'System log inspection with journalctl', 'Overview
Query binary systemd journal logs by service unit, priority level (errors/warnings), and timeframe using journalctl.

What you''ll learn
- Filtering Journal Logs
- Persistent Journal Storage

Subtopics
Filtering Journal Logs: Querying logs with journalctl -u nginx --since ''1 hour ago'' -p err.
Persistent Journal Storage: Configuring /etc/systemd/journald.conf to persist logs across server reboots.

Learning outcome
Understand system log inspection with journalctl, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Filter the system journal to view all error-level log entries generated since the last server boot.

