Prevent disk space exhaustion by configuring logrotate policies (compress, dateext, maxsize) and forward logs to central syslogs.

What you''ll learn
- Logrotate Configuration
- Rsyslog Forwarding

Subtopics
Logrotate Configuration: Writing configuration files in /etc/logrotate.d/ to compress and rotate application logs daily.
Rsyslog Forwarding: Forwarding log events over UDP/TCP to a central log server.

Learning outcome
Understand log rotation and central syslog forwarding, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Create a logrotate configuration file that rotates an application log file weekly, keeps 4 backups, and compresses old logs.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: create a logrotate configuration file that rotates an application log file weekly, keeps 4 backups, and compresses old logs. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
