INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('68533c27-7d04-5d24-820c-e98ec7ba44dc', 'ac888cc6-b3c4-58f8-966b-92989ac06356', '05b1ac42-9f16-5b17-b46c-f587f7602eaa', 'Shared responsibility model across cloud services', 'Overview
Differentiate security ''of'' the cloud (provider responsibility) from security ''in'' the cloud (customer responsibility).

What you''ll learn
- Service-Specific Boundaries
- Common Cloud Attack Vectors

Subtopics
Service-Specific Boundaries: How customer security obligations change between IaaS, PaaS, and serverless architectures.
Common Cloud Attack Vectors: Analyzing real-world cloud breaches caused by open storage buckets, SSRF, and leaked API credentials.

Learning outcome
Understand shared responsibility model across cloud services, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Analyze a cloud security incident report and identify which failures fell under customer responsibility.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: analyze a cloud security incident report and identify which failures fell under customer responsibility. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
