INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('dc7a3499-6186-53ca-aec0-1728f001e3dd', 'ac888cc6-b3c4-58f8-966b-92989ac06356', '05b1ac42-9f16-5b17-b46c-f587f7602eaa', 'Cloud threat landscape and attack surfaces', 'Overview
Explore the unique attack vectors of cloud environments including metadata service abuse, privileged role pivoting, and control plane attacks.

What you''ll learn
- Instance Metadata Service (IMDSv2)
- Control Plane vs Data Plane

Subtopics
Instance Metadata Service (IMDSv2): How IMDSv2 token-backed sessions defend against SSRF credential theft.
Control Plane vs Data Plane: Protecting cloud administrative APIs from compromised access keys and session hijacking.

Learning outcome
Understand cloud threat landscape and attack surfaces, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Verify that all cloud virtual instances require IMDSv2 and reject unauthenticated v1 metadata requests.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: verify that all cloud virtual instances require imdsv2 and reject unauthenticated v1 metadata requests. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
