INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('0b20eeff-7c8b-5927-81ed-cfb1d70e6431', 'f58d0683-af23-5413-a9ab-ad60087f0c34', 'a0e53895-cc3a-53d5-8207-e2eaa4495834', 'Kernel space vs user space architecture', 'Overview
Understand CPU privilege rings, monolithic kernel architecture, and the boundary protecting hardware from user applications.

What you''ll learn
- Privilege Rings and Context Switches
- Monolithic Kernel Design

Subtopics
Privilege Rings and Context Switches: How x86/ARM CPU rings enforce memory isolation between ring 0 (kernel) and ring 3 (user space).
Monolithic Kernel Design: How core drivers, filesystems, and network stacks execute inside shared kernel memory space.

Learning outcome
Understand kernel space vs user space architecture, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Inspect CPU execution modes and memory segmentation using lscpu and /proc/cpuinfo.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: inspect cpu execution modes and memory segmentation using lscpu and /proc/cpuinfo. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 0) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
