INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('a4c0e0eb-8f49-504b-9581-c7560e97476a', 'f58d0683-af23-5413-a9ab-ad60087f0c34', 'a0e53895-cc3a-53d5-8207-e2eaa4495834', 'Linux system call interface and glibc', 'Overview
Learn how user space programs request kernel services using software interrupts, syscall instructions, and glibc wrappers.

What you''ll learn
- The Syscall Mechanism
- Standard C Library Wrappers

Subtopics
The Syscall Mechanism: How registers pass system call numbers and arguments before switching to kernel mode.
Standard C Library Wrappers: How glibc wraps raw kernel syscalls and sets errno on failure.

Learning outcome
Understand linux system call interface and glibc, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Trace all system calls invoked by a simple command (such as ''ls'') using strace and identify the openat and read calls.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: trace all system calls invoked by a simple command (such as ''ls'') using strace and identify the openat and read calls. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
