INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('21acca92-e51e-59b1-8bed-ef208309d4c9', 'f58d0683-af23-5413-a9ab-ad60087f0c34', 'a0e53895-cc3a-53d5-8207-e2eaa4495834', 'Virtual memory, pages and swap mechanics', 'Overview
Understand virtual address spaces, Memory Management Units (MMU), page tables, 4KB memory pages, page faults, and swap.

What you''ll learn
- Virtual Memory Translation
- Page Faults and Swapping

Subtopics
Virtual Memory Translation: How the MMU translates virtual process memory addresses into physical RAM frames.
Page Faults and Swapping: Handling major vs minor page faults, demand paging, and swapping inactive pages to disk.

Learning outcome
Understand virtual memory, pages and swap mechanics, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Inspect virtual memory statistics of a process by reading /proc/[pid]/smaps and running vmstat 1 5.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: inspect virtual memory statistics of a process by reading /proc/[pid]/smaps and running vmstat 1 5. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
