INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('3814821a-265f-5e28-a6cf-7f78aeb44d69', 'f58d0683-af23-5413-a9ab-ad60087f0c34', 'a0e53895-cc3a-53d5-8207-e2eaa4495834', 'The /proc and /sys virtual filesystems', 'Overview
Interact with kernel data structures and hardware device trees exposed dynamically as text files in /proc and /sys.

What you''ll learn
- The /proc Filesystem
- The /sys (sysfs) Tree

Subtopics
The /proc Filesystem: Reading kernel runtime statistics, process maps (/proc/[pid]/maps), and hardware info (/proc/meminfo).
The /sys (sysfs) Tree: Inspecting bus hierarchies, block devices, and network interface settings exposed in sysfs.

Learning outcome
Understand the /proc and /sys virtual filesystems, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
