Master pointer arithmetic, stack frames, heap allocation (malloc, calloc, realloc, free), and prevent memory leaks.

What you''ll learn
- Pointers and Memory Addresses
- Dynamic Memory Management

Subtopics
Pointers and Memory Addresses: Dereferencing memory addresses, passing pointers to functions, and double pointers.
Dynamic Memory Management: Allocating dynamic heap memory and using Valgrind to detect memory leaks and buffer overflows.

Learning outcome
Understand memory allocation, pointers and stack vs heap, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Write a C program that dynamically allocates a resizable array of integers and verify zero memory leaks with Valgrind.

