Share memory regions directly between processes using shm_open and mmap, and synchronize access using POSIX semaphores.

What you''ll learn
- Shared Memory (shm_open, mmap)
- Semaphores and Mutexes

Subtopics
Shared Memory (shm_open, mmap): Mapping the same physical RAM frame into the virtual address spaces of two processes.
Semaphores and Mutexes: Preventing race conditions when multiple processes read and write to shared memory.

Learning outcome
Understand shared memory and semaphores, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
