INSERT INTO asgard_catalog.topics (id, roadmap_id, milestone_id, title, explanation, position) VALUES ('d4646011-fe4a-51f9-8f15-f1978f02e787', 'f58d0683-af23-5413-a9ab-ad60087f0c34', 'f4a30946-f0c7-57c6-8610-ffa03f8ca3dc', 'Tracing execution with strace and ltrace', 'Overview
Diagnose application crashes, missing configuration files, and permission denials by tracing system calls and library calls.

What you''ll learn
- Syscall Timing and Counts
- Attaching to Running Processes

Subtopics
Syscall Timing and Counts: Using strace -c to generate a summary table of syscall counts, errors, and time spent in the kernel.
Attaching to Running Processes: Attaching strace -p [pid] to live production processes to diagnose hangs.

Learning outcome
Understand tracing execution with strace and ltrace, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Trace a failing command with strace to identify the exact file path that caused a ''file not found'' or permission error.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: trace a failing command with strace to identify the exact file path that caused a ''file not found'' or permission error. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 1) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
