Profile CPU cache misses, function call overhead with perf, and explore programmable in-kernel tracing with eBPF.

What you''ll learn
- CPU Sampling with perf
- eBPF Programmable Tracing

Subtopics
CPU Sampling with perf: Recording CPU cycles with perf record and generating flame graphs to visualize hot code paths.
eBPF Programmable Tracing: How Extended Berkeley Packet Filter (eBPF) runs sandboxed bytecode safely inside the kernel for observability.

Learning outcome
Understand linux performance analysis tools (perf, ebpf basics), complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Record a CPU profile of a busy command using perf record and view the function call overhead using perf report.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: record a cpu profile of a busy command using perf record and view the function call overhead using perf report. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 2) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
