Build a production-grade C or shell systems daemon that collects /proc metrics, handles signals, and logs to systemd.

What you''ll learn
- Daemonization Standards
- Complete Systems Capstone

Subtopics
Daemonization Standards: Forking background processes, detaching controlling terminals, and redirecting standard I/O.
Complete Systems Capstone: Synthesizing process monitoring, IPC, signal handling, and kernel tuning into a reliable utility.

Learning outcome
Understand building an automated systems monitoring daemon, complete the practical exercise, and explain the key concepts.

Tools and setup
Use a free editor (such as VS Code), modern web browser, and relevant local runtime/CLI; no paid service or subscription is required for these exercises.

Practice
Deploy your systems monitoring daemon under systemd, verify clean signal termination, and review its journal logs.

Completion check
You can show and explain the outcome of: deploy your systems monitoring daemon under systemd, verify clean signal termination, and review its journal logs. Check that it functions as expected and meets requirements.', 3) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
